cool breeze wrote:
>
> I had a recent wizard, and he found a dwarvish mithril coat not far
> into the dungeon. Putting it on, I found his spell casting to be quite
> bad.

Early wizards have the tradeoff that their spell casting blows anyways
so there's a lot of sense in playing them as dagger throwers with the
best armor they can find early on.  Then later switch to worse armor in
favor of more spell casting.

> Now, as I understand from looking at some of the spoilers that
> elven mithril coat does not hamper spellcasting and even provides some
> resistances to enemy spellcasting.  My question is, is this early
> dwarven mithril coat just something to drop in a general store or is
> there some use for this usually powerful item?

The primary difference between elven and dwarvish mithril is one point
of AC better with the dwarvish with the elven being a bit more common. 
You will not gain from that switch.  Selling your spares in a shop works
well to build up your early game gold supply.

The early options for wizard tend to be dwarvish mithril and use daggers
versus studded leather armor and use daggers but also start working
towards spell skills.  It depends on how carefully you play.

There are plenty of early dwarves to supply you with mithril.  Build
your pet strong enough and you'll probably end up with studded leather
armor from a different type of monster victim.  Also experiment with
other types of armor and what they do to your spell casting.  Gather the
types that have no or little effect and at some point you'll have enough
that you can afford to switch from mithril to studded leather.


